EXECUTED WRITTEN COMMERCIAL LICENSE FROM FRACTAL COMPUTE ORCHESTRATIONS IS STRICTLY
PROHIBITED AND CONSTITUTES WILLFUL INFRINGEMENT.

3.2. Explicitly Prohibited Activities (Anti-Hosted-Service & Anti-Startup Shield):
  (a) Products, SDKs, Wrappers, & Clean-Room Commercial Ports:
      Incorporating, embedding, wrapping, porting, reimplementing using insights from the
      Work, sublicensing, packaging, or linking the Work (or any derivative work thereof)
      into any commercial software, proprietary or open-core product, SDK, library, or SaaS;
  (b) Hosted, Cloud, Managed, & Wrapper Services (Anti-Cloud-Takeover Clause):
      Operating, deploying, or making the Work (or any fork, derivative, API wrapper, or
      quantization/orchestration pipeline built atop it) accessible to third parties as a
      managed cloud service, Software-as-a-Service (SaaS), Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS),
      Inference-as-a-Service, remote RPC endpoint, or compute marketplace, whether paid,
      freemium, ad-supported, token-incentivized, or bundled with a paid offering;
  (c) Forming or Operating a Company Around the Work or Its Derivatives:
      Incorporating, founding, funding, pitching, operating, or building enterprise/equity
      value for any company, startup, corporate subsidiary, or commercial venture whose
      product, competitive advantage, infrastructure, or revenue relies upon the Work or
      derivatives/forks created after accessing the Work;
  (d) Paid Consulting, Compute Harvesting, & Commercial Model Artifacts:
      Using the Work to deliver paid consulting, integration, support contracts, model
      slicing, or federated training for third parties, OR selling/monetizing model
      checkpoints, quantized partitions (.pte / .frqd / .frq4), or telemetry outputs;
  (e) Internal Business / Enterprise Usage:
      Internal production, staging, R&D, employee tooling, or operational use inside ANY
      for-profit company, corporation, firm, or commercial entity (even if nothing is
